789 0 obj
<<
/Title (We started with the raw medicine dataset and followed a simple analytical process: clean the data, calculate relevant statistics, visualise the patterns, and interpret the findings. Each insight is based on what the cleaned data actually shows.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 735 0 R
/Prev 816 0 R
/Next 763 0 R
>>
endobj
790 0 obj
<<
/Title (The objective of this project is to transform a large Indian medicine catalogue into a clear, evidence-based data story using Python and data visualisation. Starting with 253,973 raw medicine records, we aim to clean and validate the dataset, explore its important characteristics, identify meaningful patterns, and communicate those findings through charts and statistical evidence. The analysis focuses on understanding how medicines are distributed across manufacturers, how prices are distributed, how pricing patterns vary between major manufacturers, which active ingredients appear most frequently, and how common combination formulations are. The overall goal is not simply to present numbers, but to use the data to explain the structure and patterns visible within the medicine catalogue in a simple and understandable way.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 764 0 R
/Next 817 0 R
>>
endobj
