825 0 obj
<<
/Title (Our analysis is based on the A-Z Medicine Dataset of India,  which contains 253,973 medicine records across 9 attributes. The dataset includes important fields such as the medicine or brand name, maximum retail price, manufacturer name, primary and secondary active ingredients, discontinued status, and medicine type. These variables allow us to study four major dimensions of the catalogue: manufacturer representation, price distribution, active ingredient frequency, and formulation structure. Before beginning the main analysis, we conducted an initial data-quality audit by examining the dataset structure, data types, missing values, duplicate records, and discontinued medicines. The audit identified 7,905 discontinued records, while all records were already classified as allopathy. The dataset contains 7,611 manufacturers and 7,750 distinct primary active ingredients, providing a broad base for exploring patterns across the Indian medicine catalogue.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 795 0 R
/Prev 846 0 R
>>
endobj
